{
    "background_story": "Zayd was a young man from a small, coastal village where tradition ran deep. In his community, it was customary to take a matronymic surname, honoring one's mother's lineage. Zayd's surname, Umari, was a testament to his mother's strength and influence. His mother, Um Ali, was a respected healer and leader in the village, known for her wisdom and compassion. Zayd grew up listening to stories of his mother's bravery and kindness, and he sought to emulate her example. As he came of age, Zayd took great pride in carrying his mother's name, feeling a deep connection to his maternal heritage. He went on to become a skilled sailor and navigator, always keeping his mother's memory close to his heart and striving to make her proud.",
